      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arctangent",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
