      "problem": "If ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}},$ then $f(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
